  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $S_{1}$ and $S_{2}$ be orientable surfaces of finite type. Under what\nconditions do injective maps from (finite-index subgroups of) the mapping class\ngroup of $S_{1}$ to the mapping class group of $S_{2}$ necessarily arise from “manipulations”\n(e.g., inclusions, (branched) coverings, etc.) taking $S_{1}$ to $S_{2}$?",
